{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782256404,"nonce":"IPvlmUWID4HdZ+j5pdaJT9mlO30=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGfGAnw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/315","origin":"github"},"title":"Battery turn-back trigger has no distance reserve → power exhaustion 1.29 nm from dock (2026-06-23 Massabesic)","message":"## Summary\n\nDuring the 2026-06-23 Lake Massabesic survey ([#313](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/313)), BizzyBoat **ran out of power underway and was towed in**. No low-battery warning ever fired before the shutdown.\n\n## What happened\n\n- Pack ~24 V nominal. Voltage was the only available gauge: `/bizzy/mavros/battery` reported Current = 0 and Remaining blank throughout, so there was **no SOC% and no current draw** to alarm on.\n- Voltage declined over the survey to ~20.6–20.9 V, then at **~15:51–15:52** telemetry ceased instantly — the BMS hit its critical-voltage cutoff and **shut the whole boat down at once** (operator-confirmed mechanism; not a gradual brownout).\n- The `/diagnostics` battery level stayed `OK(0)` right up to the cutoff. **No WARN/ERROR ever fired.**\n\n## Why it matters\n\nBecause the BMS cutoff is instantaneous with zero graceful degradation, there is no \"limp home\" window. An alarm is only useful if it fires with margin **above** the BMS cutoff voltage, not at it.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\n- Configure MAVROS battery plugin low/critical **voltage thresholds** + pack capacity so SOC% and a low-battery alarm work.\n- Set the alarm threshold well above the BMS hard-cutoff (define the cutoff voltage first).\n- Consider adding **current sensing** so SOC/remaining-time estimates are possible (currently Current = 0 always).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Power timeline + plot: `docs/logs/2026/2026-06-23_dev_logs.md`, `docs/logs/2026/2026-06-23_dock_departure_voltage.png` (deployment #313).\n- Voltage source: `/bizzy/mavros/battery` (boat bag `~/data/logs/gabby/logs/bizzyboat/2026-06-23T13-03-52+00-00`) and `bizzy_battery/battery_2026-06-23.csv`.\n\nRelated: #196 (charger idle current + power models). Part of #313.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}